## THE WORK
**Step 0.** `date`; `df -g`; copy this kit into `1_Project_Definition/Briefs/` (`cmp`, sha256); absolute target and hard stop; REFUSE; `Briefs/2026-11-06_B1331_STATUS.md` (first line `RECORDS B1331: PENDING`; STATUS-NOW; last line `WORKING: <step>, <time>` true after every step). Take the `*-before` files (the three dirty root files and `CLARIFICATIONS.md`, byte copies, ONCE, before any append), the Jira counts and the five keys' state ONCE. **Never `du` over `.tools`; never open, list or read any `.tools/b1*` except `b1316` (read) and `b1331`.**
**Step 1. PRIOR-WORK CHECK.** As the PRIOR WORK section. Print C-79's lines.
**Step 2.** Under `.tools/.git-lock` (atomic `mkdir`, holder file, own `rmdir`; ref writes only) `git worktree add -b records/b1331 .tools/wt-b1331-records <root HEAD>`; ONE path on the branch (`1_Project_Definition/CLARIFICATIONS.md`).
**Step 3.** Source checks to `runs/` (J1, J2, J3, J4, controls printed).
**Step 4. Jira** (only under slots). `myself` 200; freeze plan and texts; order: the create (only if MINORS-AS = TICKET), then per key in numeric order MPSCALC-107, -116, -118, -374, -375: re-read the key (status as Step 0, labels unchanged, comment total as Step 0), POST the comment, read it back (text equal, one-character mutant unequal, status unchanged, labels unchanged, total +1); THEN, only for a MOVE key, the move (HTTP 204, read back Done, label unchanged, summary and description equal, comment total +1). One write per command, logged first, stop at the first non-2xx, never write twice on an error. No write from HARD STOP minus 25. Afterward the other keys equal by hash (the written keys differ as the plan says).
**Step 5. Records.** (1) the C-entry, ONE commit naming B1331 and "C-96", trailer, never amended; (2) BACKLOG rows; (3) history entry; (4) `JIRA.md` section; (5) property check on scratch copies BEFORE any append (worktree diff only `M 1_Project_Definition/CLARIFICATIONS.md`, added lines only; the text scan `scan610` plus the Jira word list clean, planted control fires every kind; each finding id once per artifact); (6) land as R180: `merge --ff-only` under the lock, `main^{tree}` = branch tree, `refs-after.txt`, `rmdir`, `df` last. The root repo has no remote and no pull request; the CodeQL rule governs the code repository, which this pass does not touch, and nothing here bypasses or dismisses any alert.

## THE TEXTS (skeletons; build from the sources and freeze)
ASCII; `<<NAME>>` printed by program in the same action as the write; after the fill `<<` and `>>` count 0. **Fixed texts (the comments, the C-entry, the ticket, BACKLOG and history text) carry: no person's name, no decision-card id, no B-number, no finding id, none of the words seat, brief, lane, gate, tuesday, live, deployed, complet; say "independent review" for a review and "the coordinator" for the coordinator seat; no dollar sign, percent sign, backtick, or digit-dot-digit (file:line pointers, shas and three-part versions are exempt; write other figures as whole numbers); say `success` for a check-run.** The exemptions R180 took for the strings its own kit mandated ("Measured by this seat at write time", "this seat did not query the decision store", "Recorded by B1331 SEAT-R183", the row ids, finding ids in BACKLOG and JIRA.md accounting only, the ticket summary prefix `[B1325-1,2,3]`) are taken here by exact string and nowhere else; the Jira comments have no exemption. H: `The squash is merged to main only; it is not in any hosted build (relayed, not probed by this pass).` C: `Source: records pass, <<DAY>>.` No plant id appears in a comment.
**TX-MPSCALC-107 / TX-MPSCALC-116** (one each): BLUF `<<key>>: MPS #<<N>> (squash <<SQ8>>, merged <<AE>> by program), re-read from the API on the write day, an ancestor of code main <<MAIN8>>; tests only, <<paths>>. <<Moved to Done under the product owner's 1 November ruling that Done means merged to main | Recorded; not moved: <<the named unmet clause or the condition that holds it>>>>.` Rule `Done rule: the product owner's 1 November ruling, in this project's records: "Done means merged to main, the same as Composer"; a ticket moves only where every Done-when clause is met and no review line or red run stands against it (the coordinator's reading of the ruling).` Clauses `Done-when, clause by clause (the clause text is the builder's, relayed by the independent review; the ticket carries none): <<one row per clause: MET | NOT MET | NOT RE-DERIVED, with the review's mark and the code pointer>>.` Review `<<the independent review's verdict line as printed: round 1 of 2 on the class ..., NO GO 0 before; for -107 the three Minors, described in words, held as backlog rows (or as MPSCALC-<<KEY-M>> under TICKET), and whether reading (k) was applied by the stamp>>.` Check-runs `<<8 of 8 success on the squash; the Push on main and ci runs success on attempt 1 on code main; read at the write time; code-scanning shows no open alert but the read has no control that fires>>.` Open `<<what holds the ticket: for -107 the Minors; who can release it; no sentence is drafted for the product>>.` H. C. For -116 the record sentence of the review's item 3 may be quoted with "nothing is deployed" replaced by "nothing is in any hosted build".
**TX-MPSCALC-118** (ONE comment; item 3 above): BLUF `<<MPSCALC-118: not built, and not proposed again for the reason below. This is the coordinator's judgement of 2026-11-06, not a ruling by the product owner.>>` Then `Why not as filed.` the fix-shape sentence and the second-implementation reason, `Why not the narrowed form.` the eight-literals reason and what it does not hold, `What stays open.` the purchase half and why it is a presentation choice, `Where.` the pointers printed at `aa7fd175`, then H without the merge sentence (no change was made): `No change was made by this pass; the hosted build is not probed.` and C.
**TX-MPSCALC-374 / -375** (only where the gap table has a MISSING row; the added items only): BLUF `<<key>>: what the move to Done on <<date>> rests on, added to the record of comment <<id>>.` then one sentence per MISSING item, then `The move is the coordinator's judgement and is reversible on the board.` (only if item 4 was MISSING) and C.
**TK (ticket, only under MINORS-AS = TICKET; ADF, one paragraph per bold label; summary `[B1325-1,2,3] Colour guard test file: the token-set row is red on the old guard only because the export is missing, the token-definition regex sees only a token that starts a line, and the paren-depth scan in the guard is pinned by no result (test only)`; type Task; label `mpscalc-b1331`; priority and assignee read from MPSCALC-107 live and asserted equal in the plan; no figures by rule): **BLUF**, **Where** (the pointers at `aa7fd175`), **What** (the three Minors in words), **Fix shape** (quoted from the review), **Regression** (a row that observes the blanked text, or the loop removed with the suite green; the regex counts a second token on the same line), **Recorded by** `records pass B1331, <<DAY>>`.
**C-96** (slot REC-CLAR-96; ONE heading after C-95; copy C-93's and C-94's shape for a landing entry and C-94's scan paragraph): heading `### C-96 -- Did MPS #159 (the summary census renders the rental proposal and the one-pager, MPSCALC-116) and MPS #160 (the colour guard reads var() fallbacks and filter and takes a token list, MPSCALC-107) land on main? (a landing recorded by the coordinator; <<no product-owner ruling | the ruling named by RULING-REF>>)`. `Source:` a landing recorded by the coordinator, as relayed by the stamp on this kit and the independent review's STATUS (**RELAYED: this seat did not query the decision store**; no card id). `The words, verbatim as relayed:` *none new* (or the stamp's words); the Done rule's words at `CLARIFICATIONS.md:1714`. `Measured by this seat at write time` (J1 for both, the tables, the Jira before and after, controls, what the weak zero was). `Settles:` nothing is ruled; the two squashes stand on main as they are; the moves, if any, rest on C-79 and the stamp slots alone. `Delivered:` comment ids, moves or reasons, the rows or the new key, the 118 comment, the gap result; BACKLOG rows by pointer. `Not settled:` the hosted build; the three Minors; the purchase half of MPSCALC-118; any gap the table found in -374 or -375. `Note on order:` C-numbers follow the order of recording; C-96 follows C-95; C-97 is next by program. `C-scan at write time` (highest heading before the commit, branch count, zero for the ANCHORED `^### C-96( |$)`; after the commit: highest heading C-96 found once; `^### C-95( |$)` once; `^### C-97( |$)` 0; the earlier lines (2581 at drafting, you print yours) byte-equal to the root file by `cmp` on `head -n <that count>`; a one-byte mutant unequal), and `Recorded by B1331 SEAT-R183 (records), 2026-11-06, from the relayed words and the sources.` ASCII.

## FENCES, PARTITION, HOLDS
- **Git:** only `worktree add -b`, ONE commit, ONE `merge --ff-only`; reads `--no-optional-locks`; no `git add` in the dirty root, stash, reset, clean, rebase, amend, fetch, push; `2_Project_Files` untouched (read origin by `gh api -X GET` only; the local code checkout is stale).
- **Jira:** only under the slots; bodies frozen first; fence tests printed; the five keys (plus the one create) only.
- **PARTITION (both sides).** No MPS builder or gate is live (no `Datasec/MPS-` pane at drafting); a new MPS seat may start while you work, and the one shared thing is `.tools/.git-lock` (poll as REFUSE 6). HPSM-POC seats (`HPSM-POC-G354`, `HPSM-POC-H131` at drafting) write HPSM-POC paths only, in another repository. **You write only the root records repo (branch `records/b1331`, `.tools/b1331`, `.tools/wt-b1331-records`, the Briefs copy, your STATUS, the three appended root files, `CLARIFICATIONS.md` on the branch) and Jira (the stamped comments, the stamped moves, the one stamped create).** You never touch a code path, branch, pull request or alert. Project counts after: 384 issues (385 with the create); Done 152 plus the moves; information only.
- **HOLDS (standing lines):** **PRIOR-WORK CHECK is a standing line** (a READY without a PRIOR WORK section is returned). **No message to any human** (no mail, no chat, no comment addressed to a named person). **Jira writes only where this kit's scope says.** **Never delete** (quarantine to `.tools/b1331/_quarantine/`). Nothing outside the five keys and the root records files; no code, register or contract change; no deploy claim; no HTTP except Jira and `gh api -X GET` under the project `GH_CONFIG_DIR`; no hosted site (not even a GET), no `az`, ssh, docker, tests, build, npm, port; never type `cd`; quote the project path; no assignee or label change on an existing ticket; no wording drafted for the product. This pass builds nothing.
- **STATUS:** as R180's plus `df` at start, after Step 2 and at end, PRIOR WORK, the J1 landings, the pointer tables, the two DONE-WHEN tables, the contradiction check per key, the gap table, the 118 pointers, every write with its read-back. **FOR TUESDAY** 1: the landing lines and the commit (any red run first); 2: per key, the comment id and the move or the named unmet clause, with what would release it; the Minors as rows or the new key; 3: one line exactly `decision_queue.sh --delivered <CARD-REF from the stamp> "<n> comments; <moved keys or none>; C-96"` with values printed by program (skip if CARD-REF is NONE); 4: any move of code main; 5: where you followed this kit although a source reads differently, and why, and any clause of -374 or -375 you read unmet. **Last line exactly one of:** `READY FOR REVIEW: B1331 | root main <sha8> -> <sha8> (ff-only) | C-96 | creates <n> | comments <n> | transitions <n> | MPSCALC total <n>, Done <n> | text scan 0 | no push` | `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>` | `BLOCKED: <reason>` | `WORKING: ...`.

